WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.570
It was one of the longest relationships of my

00:00:02.570 --> 00:00:05.240
life, and certainly one of the happiest.

00:00:06.170 --> 00:00:08.510
The repairman confirmed my suspicion.

00:00:08.510 --> 00:00:10.160
The manifold valve and the right front

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.870
burner had rusted through.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.630
I guess everyone remembers where they were

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:17.240
when Kitchen King discontinued their deluxe

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.950
six burner flattop.

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:22.020
I'm sorry, I cannot publish this.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:22.730
Too long?

00:00:22.850 --> 00:00:24.110
Does it come with a forklift?

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:25.250
Thank you, Terry.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:28.150
No, it's not just about the length, Adrian.

00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:31.310
We hired you to write about your career as a

00:00:31.310 --> 00:00:32.540
police detective.

00:00:32.570 --> 00:00:35.440
You solved 140 homicides.

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.730
That's the story we paid for.

00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:39.050
Not this. Oh.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:42.680
Here in chapter four, you have two

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:47.570
paragraphs about the suspect and seven,

00:00:47.600 --> 00:00:52.890
eight, nine pages about his vacuum cleaner.

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:54.890
We have the same vacuum cleaner, the exact

00:00:54.890 --> 00:00:57.470
same model. What are the odds of that?

00:00:58.520 --> 00:00:59.300
1 in.

00:00:59.300 --> 00:00:59.690
6?

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.460
Terence.

00:01:01.460 --> 00:01:02.870
Maybe I need an editor.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:06.020
You've had five editors and two ghost

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:07.670
writers. They all quit.

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.860
The last one changed his name and moved to

00:01:09.860 --> 00:01:12.610
Guam. I've talked to the lawyers.

00:01:12.620 --> 00:01:14.360
You're illegally in breach.

00:01:14.390 --> 00:01:16.190
We need our advance back.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.330
Advance, you mean? You mean the money?

00:01:20.340 --> 00:01:21.630
It's not my decision.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.620
I'm sorry. Adrian.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:26.700
No no no no no, you can't do that.

00:01:26.730 --> 00:01:30.510
Here's the thing. Molly's getting married in

00:01:30.510 --> 00:01:32.160
six weeks. Molly?

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:33.570
Trudy's daughter.

00:01:33.570 --> 00:01:36.210
I didn't even know about her until 12 years

00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.530
ago. It's all in the book.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.800
I mean, it will be in volume two.

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:44.250
Is there something wrong with the chair?

00:01:44.250 --> 00:01:46.020
It's not plum with cherries.

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:47.130
It should be plum.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:49.410
Maybe you could lower yours.

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:51.900
Why? To make it plum.

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.250
You'll thank me later.

00:01:54.810 --> 00:01:56.250
Oh, please don't.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:58.650
You got to pull up on the lever.

00:01:58.820 --> 00:02:00.390
Good.

00:02:00.690 --> 00:02:02.550
Maybe I'll just stand.

00:02:02.640 --> 00:02:04.410
Maybe we should all stand.

00:02:08.750 --> 00:02:10.940
Here's the thing, Molly is all I have.

00:02:10.970 --> 00:02:12.440
She's all I have left.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.960
She practically saved my life.

00:02:15.230 --> 00:02:17.840
When Covid hit, I was in pretty bad shape.

00:02:18.350 --> 00:02:19.930
Molly moved in with me.

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:22.370
She never left my side for a year and a

00:02:22.370 --> 00:02:26.420
half. She's only ever asked me for one thing

00:02:26.630 --> 00:02:28.340
. To pay for her wedding.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:30.590
I'll do whatever you want. I'll rewrite the

00:02:30.590 --> 00:02:30.830
book.

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:31.920
I'm sorry, Adrian.

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.320
It's just too late. It's been ten years.

00:02:34.340 --> 00:02:37.160
The name Adrian Monk used to mean something.

00:02:37.160 --> 00:02:38.700
It's a different world now.

00:02:38.720 --> 00:02:40.220
Everyone's moved on.

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:42.260
I have an idea.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.730
May I make a suggestion?

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:48.080
You both leave the room and someone

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:51.290
different comes in and says different things

00:02:51.290 --> 00:02:52.010
to me.

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.800
That's not going to happen.

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:58.650
How about this? You leave the room and nobody

00:02:58.650 --> 00:02:59.850
comes back in.

00:03:00.770 --> 00:03:01.520
Ever.

00:03:01.940 --> 00:03:03.290
I think we're done here.

00:03:03.770 --> 00:03:05.600
Our lawyers will be in touch.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:17.820
Adrian. What are you doing?

00:04:19.020 --> 00:04:24.930
Nothing. Let's back away.

00:04:27.470 --> 00:04:29.990
Take a step away from the window.

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:37.410
Here we go. Adrian.

00:04:38.560 --> 00:04:40.570
You have to stop thinking about that.

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:43.210
But now they're taking the money back.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:48.620
Yes. I know I was there.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:49.940
It was for her wedding.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:51.830
I promised Molly.

00:04:52.280 --> 00:04:53.390
I'm so.

00:04:54.710 --> 00:04:55.790
I'm just so.

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:07.680
Going down?

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:22.840
The wedding is off.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:24.520
Excuse me

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:45.010
? Hey.

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:52.160
Sorry. Excuse me.

00:05:52.200 --> 00:05:53.310
I'm sorry. Excuse me.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.620
Okay. I checked the board and they just

00:05:55.620 --> 00:05:56.220
landed.

00:05:56.990 --> 00:05:58.610
Where did you get this? I've ruined

00:05:58.610 --> 00:05:59.180
everything.

00:05:59.220 --> 00:06:01.580
Adrian, for the hundredth time, it's fine.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:03.350
You did us a favor. I always wanted a small

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:03.650
wedding.

00:06:04.250 --> 00:06:05.480
Oh, Molly.You don't have to say that.

00:06:05.480 --> 00:06:07.250
It's true. The backyard is going to be

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:09.440
perfect. And Griffin is, frankly relieved

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:10.910
because now he doesn't have to invite his

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:12.050
cousins from hell.

00:06:13.340 --> 00:06:14.030
Okay.

00:06:19.630 --> 00:06:20.710
Better safe. Thank you very much.

00:06:20.740 --> 00:06:20.950
Wow.

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:24.040
Look at that. They were handing these out.

00:06:24.610 --> 00:06:26.200
Everybody's you.

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:28.300
They're going to hate it.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:32.400
Oh, I think I see her.

00:06:33.580 --> 00:06:38.560
Hey! Molly! So good to see you.

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:41.290
Okay, let's see it. Okay.

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:42.070
Okay, okay.

00:06:42.080 --> 00:06:43.870
Oh a tattoo.

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:45.370
Yeah. Okay, I love it.

00:06:45.730 --> 00:06:46.780
Griffin has one too.

00:06:46.990 --> 00:06:48.190
At least you won't lose it, right?

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:53.140
Oh. There he is.

00:06:53.160 --> 00:06:54.270
Hello, boss.

00:06:54.450 --> 00:06:55.170
I've missed you.

00:06:55.170 --> 00:06:56.430
Natalie.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.770
You can't still be mad at me.

00:06:59.280 --> 00:07:01.230
What was I supposed to do?

00:07:01.260 --> 00:07:02.370
Steven transferred.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:03.570
I had to leave.

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:04.710
We've talked about this.

00:07:04.740 --> 00:07:06.510
People commute from Atlanta.

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:09.780
I thought you'd be happy for me.

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:12.050
Please be happy for me.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.740
I have a wonderful life.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:15.910
Really? Julie lives ten minutes away.

00:07:15.930 --> 00:07:18.000
I sold 27 houses last year.

00:07:18.030 --> 00:07:18.540
I'm my

00:07:18.540 --> 00:07:20.330
Own boss. Adrian.

00:07:20.360 --> 00:07:24.300
Adrian. This woman was your assistant for 12

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:25.950
years. Which is a record that will never,

00:07:25.950 --> 00:07:27.120
ever be broken.

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:29.310
So, say I'm so glad you're here.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:31.440
I'm so glad you're here.

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:32.430
Say I've missed you.

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:34.840
I have missed you.

00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:36.000
Oh, thank you, Mr.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.540
Monk. I missed you, too.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:38.860
Oh. Oh.

00:07:39.030 --> 00:07:40.920
Where's Leland? Oh, he just texted.

00:07:40.920 --> 00:07:41.940
He couldn't get off work.

00:07:41.940 --> 00:07:42.980
I thought he retired.

00:07:42.990 --> 00:07:45.270
He did for about 20 minutes, and then he took

00:07:45.270 --> 00:07:47.160
another gig. But nobody knows what he's

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:48.330
doing. It's top secret.

00:07:48.500 --> 00:07:50.430
Oh. Oh. Randy.

00:07:50.460 --> 00:07:52.730
Hey, stranger. Hey.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:55.140
Wow. You look great.

00:07:55.240 --> 00:07:57.390
So good to see you. Oh, hey, are you ready

00:07:57.390 --> 00:08:00.270
for this? I guess face your own sensor,

00:08:00.270 --> 00:08:01.590
love. You have to stay and help with the

00:08:01.590 --> 00:08:02.070
baby.

00:08:02.070 --> 00:08:03.780
I heard Benji is a dad.

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:04.800
Congrats, grandpa.

00:08:05.280 --> 00:08:05.910
Step-grandpa!

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:07.760
Okay, okay, let's see some pictures.

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:09.600
Come on, let's see it.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.540
Oh, that's not all.

00:08:12.540 --> 00:08:14.370
Guess who is just re-elected sheriff of

00:08:14.370 --> 00:08:16.070
Summit, New Jersey for the third time.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:17.190
It's no big deal.

00:08:17.190 --> 00:08:17.550
Oh.

00:08:18.300 --> 00:08:19.730
Hey, Monk, how you doing?

00:08:19.740 --> 00:08:21.720
Are you here to apologize?

00:08:22.140 --> 00:08:23.490
No, I'm here for the wedding.

00:08:23.490 --> 00:08:25.260
Oh, he thinks we abandoned him.

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.450
It was more of a betrayal, actually.

00:08:27.450 --> 00:08:29.400
But you told me to take the job you

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:30.030
recommended me.

00:08:30.060 --> 00:08:31.410
Maybe I wasn't thinking straight.

00:08:31.410 --> 00:08:33.450
Maybe I was distracted by the knife in my

00:08:33.450 --> 00:08:34.070
back.

00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:35.850
Okay. I need your help.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.530
Will you go get my bag? It's right over

00:08:37.530 --> 00:08:38.490
here. It's black.

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:39.960
How's he doing?

00:08:40.080 --> 00:08:41.370
It's hard to say.

00:08:41.370 --> 00:08:43.290
You know, after he solved Trudy's murder, he

00:08:43.290 --> 00:08:44.760
was doing better. I mean, you guys were

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:45.360
there. He was.

00:08:45.360 --> 00:08:46.110
He was just functioning.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:48.000
He was functioning more or less.

00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:50.160
But then the pandemic hit, and it was just

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:51.540
boom. Back to square one.

00:08:52.290 --> 00:08:55.650
I mean, he didn't leave the house for two

00:08:55.650 --> 00:08:58.680
years. And then he started taking those

00:08:58.680 --> 00:08:59.760
in-home rapid tests.

00:08:59.760 --> 00:09:01.020
And it was like an addiction.

00:09:01.020 --> 00:09:03.420
He was testing himself every 20 minutes.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:05.550
I'm pretty sure that cocaine would have been

00:09:05.550 --> 00:09:06.660
a cheaper habit.

00:09:08.400 --> 00:09:10.830
Then about three weeks ago, they cancelled

00:09:10.830 --> 00:09:11.960
his book deal. No.

00:09:11.970 --> 00:09:13.980
Yeah. And now I'm more worried than ever.

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:16.260
What do you mean? Well, it's just like he's

00:09:16.260 --> 00:09:18.810
giving up. I mean, he hardly talks anymore.

00:09:18.840 --> 00:09:20.580
He just sits around all day and stares out

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:22.440
the window. What are you doing?

00:09:22.470 --> 00:09:23.880
You'll thank me later.

